@rekram1-node happens using the server from `import { createOpencodeServer } from '@opencode-ai/sdk';`

and sending the request using 

```
import { createOpencodeClient } from '@opencode-ai/sdk';

const baseUrl = await ensureOpenCodeServer(this.configuredBaseUrl); // this return an instance of createOpencodeServer
const client = createOpencodeClient({ baseUrl });
const promptResult = await client.session.promptAsync({
        path: { id: sessionId },
        body: {
          parts: [{ type: 'text', text: userText }],
          tools: toolsMap,
          system,
          ...(parsedModel ? { model: parsedModel } : {})
        }
      });
```

for the model i am using minimax m2.5 free, if i do a rollback, reasoning works, but if i back to the latest release, the server keeps me waiting until get everything as text included the reasoning

Note: i am in discord if u need more details would love to fix this providing any detail

previously I'd checked making manual curl requests to my MCP server that it was returning the outputSchema with descriptions, and asked the LLM in opencode for full description it had of the MCP tool, and if it sees "string from description of output parameter" anywhere in it's context, and it said it didn't see the string, and the description it returned was the tool description without anything about the outputSchema. then I searched issues for outputSchema and found https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/21591 where someone (well with emdash so probably an llm) says "opencode doesn't use outputSchema — it only reads inputSchema in convertMcpTool()".

and just now to be completely sure I ran opencode through mitmproxy, and for the MCP tool it is sending:
```
{
            "type": "function",
            "name": "mcp_tool_name",
            "description": "tool description",
            "parameters": {
                    ...info from inputSchema here...
            }
},
```
but the outputSchema is not present, and searching the strings from the descriptions in the outputSchema with mitmproxy they are not being sent at all
